# Individual-only voice (course-wide)

This course is **individual format**. Every exercise, prompt, instruction, and rubric must be solo.

## Banned phrases — never use

- "your group" / "as a group"
- "your team" / "as a team"
- "appoint a notetaker"
- "round-robin"
- "pair up" / "with a partner"
- "partner challenges your…"
- "peer red-team"
- "breakout" / "breakout session"
- "report back to the room"
- "rotate roles"
- "the group's deliverable"
- "group insights"

## Required substitutions

| Old (group) | New (solo) |
|---|---|
| "Breakout group exercise" | "Individual exercise" |
| "Discuss with your group" | "Write your answer" |
| "Group deliverable" | "Your deliverable" |
| "Present to the room" | "Post in `#ai-pm-cohort`" |
| "Volunteer groups present" | "Optional async showcase — Loom + repo URL" |
| "Group insights" | "Build Insights — 1 friction, 1 learning, 1 aha" |

## Required structure for every exercise

Every individual exercise must include, in order:

1. **Time-box** — e.g., "20m solo"
2. **Open-the-tool step** — name the specific HTML tool
3. **Self-review checklist** — 3–6 verifiable bullets
4. **AI-review prompt** — a verbatim prompt the learner pastes into ChatGPT/Claude/Cursor with their artifact
5. **Async share** — commit to the named folder in `juno-project-template/`, optionally post link in `#ai-pm-cohort`

## Final showcase voice

The original 30-minute live group showcase is rewritten as:
- **Async, individual, optional.** 3-minute Loom + repo URL posted in `#ai-pm-cohort`.
- Instructor responds in-thread within ~5 days.
- Not required for certification.

## Submission voice

- Submission = the URL of the learner's `juno-pm/` fork.
- Window = 7 days post-cohort.
- Each learner submits individually. No "the group submits."
